course: dictionary
lesson: 11449
title: Adjacent: next to each other
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: «Adjacent» means next to something, or very near to it. When two things are adjacent, there is nothing big between them. «The bathroom is adjacent to Sam's bedroom», so you can walk from one room straight into the other.
explain: You can check the meaning with context. Read «The café is adjacent to the library.» Ask yourself: what word would fit here? Words like next to or beside fit, so adjacent must mean next to.
explain: In maths, adjacent sides and adjacent angles are next to each other too. They share a side or a corner (called a vertex). A rectangle's adjacent sides meet at a corner, one long side and one short side.
fact: «Adjacent» means next to something or very near it.
fact: In maths, adjacent sides or angles share a side or a corner (vertex).
fact: Adjacent sides of a rectangle meet at a corner.
fact: Opposite sides of a rectangle do not touch, so they are not adjacent.
fact: Useful phrase: «adjacent to», as in «the car park adjacent to the school».
exercise: «The bathroom is adjacent to Sam's bedroom.» What does adjacent mean? | Far away from | Inside | *Next to, or very near | Painted the same colour as
exercise: In a rectangle, which sides are adjacent? | A side with no corners | The longest side only | *The two sides that meet at a corner | The two sides that face each other across the shape
exercise: «The café is adjacent to the library.» Which word means nearly the same as adjacent? | Upstairs | *Beside | Hidden | Distant
test: «The shop is adjacent to the park.» Where is the shop? | Very far from the park | Under the park | Inside the park | *Next to the park
test: Two angles share an arm and a corner. What are they called? | Opposite angles | Parallel angles | Right angles | *Adjacent angles
exam: «The school hall is adjacent to the kitchen, so the lunches are quick to carry.» What does adjacent tell us? | The hall is far from the kitchen | The hall and kitchen are the same size | The hall is inside the kitchen | *The hall is next to the kitchen
